Patch: 010-repair-before-any-turn
Reason: a call the rollout has no output for gets its output from the log whenever a thread resumes, before any turn is sent, not only under a recovery note: a turn that ended without answering a call (one interrupted mid-call, or settled instead of resumed) left it dangling, and the provider refuses a history with a call unanswered; the cut-off exec is answered first, as a custom tool output built from its nested calls, and the generic output is only for every other call; what a completed never call answers later in the same turn is armed only when a recovery note resumes that turn, so a new turn that calls it again runs it
Upstream: ours
Pins: a crash inside a never tool's call, then the turn closed in the log: the next send answers the dangling call from the log before the new turn, and the call is never run again
Pins: a cut-off code-mode exec is answered with a custom tool output holding the nested outcomes, and never with a generic one
Pins: a settled turn whose exec dangles with a completed never call does not answer a new turn's same call as recorded earlier: the new call runs
